meta {
  name: AI Review One Resolution
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: http://localhost:8088/api/admin-product/resolutions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/ai-review
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Hands one row to the LLM reviewer immediately, rather than waiting for the
  nightly batch.

  The verdict is always stored: it lands on `aiReview`/`aiConfidence` and is
  appended to the `decisions` log, whether or not the AI was allowed to act on
  it. Whether it *acts* depends on `resolution.automation.ai`:

  - `dryRun` — recorded, but nothing acted on.
    `notExecutedReason: "dry_run"`.
  - `confidence: "high"` plus `executeActions` — carried out through the ordinary
    action path, as actor `ai`. The action path writes its own decision entry.
  - `merge_into` / `split`, or accepting an unexecuted duplicate proposal, also
    need `executeDestructive` — those delete or move products.
  - anything less than `high` stays advisory: the row remains pending with the
    recommendation stored for a one-click apply.

  `notExecutedReason` says which of those applied. `stale` means the row changed
  while the model was thinking (a re-scrape, or you decided it first) and the
  recommendation was discarded rather than applied to a different question.
}
